# Shell scripts must stay LF — the plugin's scripts/agent-wt/*.sh run via
# git-bash on Windows and (for adopting projects) Linux CI runners. A CRLF
# leak on Windows checkout breaks them with `\r` parse errors. Pin LF so
# core.autocrlf=true can't rewrite them. (Mirrors the same fix in VeHagita's
# .gitattributes, the source this plugin's worktree scripts were ported from.)
*.sh text eol=lf

# docs/*.md must stay LF too — check-docs-drift.mjs's catalog-block/index
# comparisons normalize \r\n on both sides now (BL-1), so a CRLF checkout no
# longer makes the gate permanently red, but pinning LF here is defense in
# depth: it stops core.autocrlf from ever reintroducing the mismatch on a
# Windows checkout in the first place.
*.md text eol=lf
